    "created_at": "2021-10-01T09:05:07Z",
    "updated_at": "2021-10-01T09:05:07Z",
    "body": "I would personally not use `<embed>` over `<iframe>`. Web pages may, and that's an issue for extensions, which cannot easily communicate with the right frame without `.contentWindow`.\r\n\r\nIn https://github.com/w3c/webextensions/issues/12, there is a request for an extension API to allow extensions to communicate between content scripts (i.e. extension scripts that run in an execution environment that differs from the web page itself). Since extensions may operate on arbitrary pages, they may encounter `<embed>` elements.\r\n\r\nWithout `.contentWindow` on `<embed>`, the new extension API would not only need to accept `WindowProxy`, but also `HTMLEmbedElement`. And for consistency, also (i)frame and object elements.\r\n\r\nWith `.contentWindow` on `<embed>`, the new extension API can just take `WindowProxy`, without the need of being aware of `<embed>` or any other HTML element.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/html/issues/comments/932054590/reactions",
      "total_count": 0,
